      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "Therefore, the aim of this study was to conduct a meta-analysis to describe and summarize the current reinfection rates in different regions and among diverse populations. Furthermore, the study sought to examine trends in reinfection rates over time",
      "reason": "The review objective(s) are explicitly stated (conduct meta-analysis to describe/summarize reinfection rates; examine trends over time), but they are not clearly formulated using a relevant question-formulation framework."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_4_e2",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a meta-analysis of incidence/reinfection rates using observational study data; no planned intervention comparisons using PICO (or a variant) are described in the retrieved evidence."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 71
}

{
  "item_id": "PRISMA_2020_5",
  "elements": [
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e1",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The inclusion criteria were: (1) Conformed to research questions, i.e., studies that estimated the reinfection rate of SARS-CoV-2 or we could calculate it based on the data provided in the paper; (2) The study design included cohort study, case-control study, and descriptive study; (3) The study fited our working definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection. ... reinfection working definition in this study was based on a positive laboratory result at least 90 days after laboratory confirmation of primary infection(laboratory testing methods include reverse transcription-polymerase chain reaction or rapid antigen test, also called Lateral Flow Devices, and so on), advised from WHO and US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention [21, 22].",
      "reason": "The manuscript specifies key study characteristics for eligibility (research question match, eligible study designs, and a reinfection working definition including a ≥90-day interval and laboratory test types). However, other elements required by this criterion (e.g., explicit settings/other framework components and follow-up requirements) are not fully specified in the retrieved evidence."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "To avoid language bias, the search was not limited to any language. We conducted preliminary screening based on the English title and English abstract provided by nonEnglish articles.",
      "reason": "Language criteria are addressed (search not limited by language). However, the retrieved evidence does not specify other report-characteristic eligibility criteria such as dissemination year or publication/report status."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "There is no retrieved evidence that the review distinguishes exclusions where outcomes were not measured versus exclusions where outcome results were not reported."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e4",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "In addition, considering the change in the reinfection rate over time, we constructed a multiple meta-regression using the time interval between two positive tests as the independent variable, to estimate the time-varying reinfection rate. Subgroup analyses were performed by meta-regression to fit stratified rates of reinfection based on variables such as variant and country, and we also used spline regression to fit time-varying reinfection rates that did not account for heterogeneity.",
      "reason": "The retrieved evidence describes how analyses were stratified/grouped (e.g., by variant and country) and includes an analysis approach for time-varying rates. However, it does not explicitly state the groups used in each synthesis in a way that is clearly linked to specific comparisons defined in the review objectives."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_5_e5",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "To avoid language bias, the search was not limited to any language. ... Moreover, there is still no clear global definition of SARS-CoV-2 reinfection. Some studies defined reinfection as the time interval between two positive tests needing to be more than 90 days [16, 17], while some studies defined reinfection as the time interval only needing to be more than 30 days [18, 19], and it was difficult to directly compare reinfection rates under different definitions with large differences [20]. Therefore, the aim of this study was to conduct a meta-analysis to describe and summarize the current reinfection rates in different regions and among diverse populations.",
      "reason": "The manuscript provides rationale for notable eligibility/review restrictions/choices (e.g., no language restriction to avoid language bias; use of a specific reinfection working definition given the lack of global definition and the difficulty comparing different interval definitions). Not all notable restrictions and their rationales are fully captured in the retrieved evidence."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 67
}

